  "body": "This adds a way for the panel widget to be collapsed.\r\n\r\nThis feature was first skipped because of time constraint when releasing InstantSearch.js 3. This is a missing feature that was possible to implement in v2.\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n- Set the panel as \"collapsible\"\r\n- Set the panel as \"collapsible\" with a collapsed state by default\r\n- Drive the collapsed state with the helper state (fixes #2083)\r\n\r\n## Usage\r\n\r\n```js\r\nsearch.addWidget(\r\n  instantsearch.widgets.panel({\r\n    collapsed: options => {\r\n      return options && options.state && options.state.query.length === 0;\r\n    },\r\n    templates: {\r\n      header: 'Collapsible panel',\r\n      footer: 'Footer',\r\n    },\r\n  })(instantsearch.widgets.refinementList)({\r\n    container,\r\n    attribute: 'brand',\r\n  })\r\n);\r\n```\r\n\r\n## API\r\n\r\nThis introduces a new option in the `panel` widget called `collasped`.\r\n\r\n`collasped`\r\n\r\n> `SearchParameters => boolean` | no default\r\n\r\nWhen this function is defined, it marks the panel as \"collapsible\". When the panel is collapsible, we add the CSS classes defined in the [Panel specs](https://instantsearch-css.netlify.com/widgets/panel/).\r\n\r\n### Uncontrolled mode\r\n\r\nTo always collapse the panel:\r\n\r\n```js\r\npanel({\r\n  // ...\r\n  collapsed: () => false,\r\n})\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo collapse the panel until a query is typed:\r\n\r\n```js\r\npanel({\r\n  collapsed: options => {\r\n    return options && options.state && options.state.query.length === 0;\r\n  },\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Controlled mode\r\n\r\nOnce the user starts interacting with the panel (with the ➕ and ➖ buttons), the panel enters in a controlled mode. It no longer reacts to the search parameters sent to the `collapsed` function.\r\n\r\n## Stories\r\n\r\n- [Collapsed panel](https://deploy-preview-3575--instantsearchjs.netlify.com/stories/?selectedKind=Panel&selectedStory=with%20collapsed&full=0&addons=1&stories=1&panelRight=0&addonPanel=storybook%2Factions%2Factions-panel)",
